# Symbols found by the level-2 bench area (2026-10-27): level 2's data in the main code and the routines its
# bench runs reached. Format: ADDRESS NAME [comment], with +entry and +code lines, as analysis/main_8000.sym.
# The main code ($8000-$125FF) is byte-identical in build/ram/level1_full.bin and level2_full.bin, so these
# names may seed either image; the data they name is level 2's (header +0..+39 at $868C).
# Sources: REA (Ghidra provider, raw-binary m68k, entry 0x0, build/ram/level2_full.bin sha256 a039a158...,
# seeds analysis/ghidra_seeds.tsv sha256 c4accf3d...): procedure_assembly of $8582, $871A, $FFC4, $C25C, $C868,
# $D1E2, $9EE8, $8F02 (pseudo code), $9150 and $91BC (pseudo code), read_bytes of $8664, $86FA, $8FC0, $91B0,
# $97B0, $C91A, $D1C4; xrefs of $16D0, $8054-$805A, $D1CA, $D1DC; and the bench runs of this area
# (l2bench.py / l2cov.py: who wrote $16D0, the code-area writes, the executed blocks).

# --- the per-level load table and the level-2 entry
86dc  level_restart_rts    rts: the load table's restart entries [1]-[3] (levels 2 and 3 after a death or a continue: nothing reloaded)
868c  level_header_1       level 2's header (40 bytes): objlist $A828, hazards $95B2, specials $8FE0, spawnlist $97B0, start (352, 784), relocation (192, 112), markers $C5EC, camera_y_max $270, timer $0730, spawn delay $2E, marker mask 7, palette $10036

# --- level 2's special objects (update_special_objects $8B32, list $8FE0 = header +8)
8fe0  speclist_level1      9 record pointers then -1: 5 lifts, 4 trolleys
9088  sp1_lift0            lift x $AE, y $315, path $2C5 $315 (2 stops; waits at a stop until RoboCop rides it)
9098  sp1_lift1            lift x $21E, path $275 $2C5 $315 (3 stops)
90aa  sp1_lift2            lift x $9EE, path $1D5 $2C5 $315 (moves by itself when nobody rides: period 320 game frames)
90bc  sp1_lift3            lift x $EF, path $134 $1D4 (moves by itself: period 160)
90cc  sp1_lift4            lift x $9EF, path $A5 $135 $185 (moves by itself)
90de  sp1_trolley0         trolley ($8F02) over vat 0: x $340, y $250, path x $350 <-> $3F0 (2 px a frame, period 160)
90ee  sp1_trolley1         trolley over vat 1: x $510, path $518 <-> $580 (period 104)
90fe  sp1_trolley2         trolley over vat 2: x $628, path $628 <-> $6B0 (period 136)
910e  sp1_trolley3         trolley over vat 3: x $7E0, y $280, path $7E0 <-> $8B0 (period 208)

# --- level 2's hazards: the vats
91b0  level_tick_table     BRA.W per level from $9150 (records in the camera window): $933A beams, $91BC vats, $9436 (level 3)
95b2  hazards_level1       7 vats x 8 bytes (x0, y, x1, rows), -1: (848-1024, 640) (1296-1440, 640) (1568-1712, 640) (2016-2256, 688) (1904-2240, 288) (1264-1568, 288) (608-800, 288)
92da  vat_phases           22 words in the code area (never reset): low byte + 2 every other frame for the first vat in view ($15F0), bits 1-3 the surface frame; high byte $80 = the second tile set ($927A/$929A/$92BA)
927a  vat_tiles            three 16-word tables of map words for the vats' surface (top, rows, bottom)

# --- level 2's objects reached on the bench
c91a  obj02_arrest         Cain's tail after his draw (obj02_update pushes it with pea before the computed jmp at $C90E, so Ghidra's body stops at $C916): hit points (+$21) pinned at 4 every frame; touched (+$23): message $DC8A, sound $21 ($B2C), $16D0 set (level done, at $C936), $16C4 = $40; D0 = -1
+entry c91a
dc76  msg_arrest_armed     "ARREST ARMED EMEMY." (obj02 queues it every 64 game frames, $C870)
dc8a  msg_arrest_ok        "ARREST SUCESSFUL." (obj02_arrest: the end of level 2)
c25c  kill_case_c25c       update_objects' kill switch ($C42A) case: objects $12-$14 by $C398, three explosions, $16D0 set, $16C4 = $40, message $C24B "CAIN DESTROYED." (not executed in any level-2 bench run)
